// Splash Counter Pipeline — generates and deploys a native counter app
// via the Makepad/Splash UI framework.
//
// Flow:
//   generate_app ──→ deploy_app
//
// Tool contract:
//   launch_app   — sends Splash DSL body to the Makepad host for rendering
//   message      — sends text responses back to the user through the channel

digraph splash_counter {
    graph [label="Splash Counter App Pipeline", default_model="splash-counter"]

    // --- Generate the Splash counter app using the fake provider ---
    generate_app [
        handler="codergen",
        prompt="You are a native UI generator. Generate a Splash DSL counter application.

The user wants a simple counter app with:
- A window with title 'octos Counter'
- A numeric display showing the current count
- Increment (+) and decrement (-) buttons
- A reset button
- A 'Say Hello' button that sends a message back to the agent via __pi_response.set_text()

The app must use Splash DSL syntax with:
- App { } as root
- Window { } with title, width, height
- Body { } with padding and spacing
- VStack and HStack for layout
- Button widgets with name attributes for event handling
- Text widgets with name attributes for rendering dynamic values
- State { } block declaring the count variable
- Action: blocks for each button

Output ONLY the Splash DSL body. No markdown, no explanation.",
        label="Generate App",
        model="splash-counter",
        timeout_secs="60"
    ]

    // --- Deploy the app to the Makepad host ---
    deploy_app [
        handler="codergen",
        prompt="You are a native UI deployer. Deploy the Splash app to the Makepad host.

Use the output from the previous node as the Splash DSL body.

Call the launch_app tool with the Splash DSL body to render it in a native window.

After launching, tell the user the app is running with instructions on how to interact with it.

Available tools: launch_app, message",
        label="Deploy App",
        model="splash-counter",
        tools="message",
        timeout_secs="120"
    ]

    // --- Edges ---
    generate_app -> deploy_app
}
